P2
# hubot demo world -- PLAIN TEXT (PGM "P2", ASCII). Not the mask; this is the map
# the costmap's static_layer reads, and it exists for one measured reason:
# 
#   CostmapFilter::updateBounds() ignores all four of its bounds arguments. If no
#   PLUGIN declares a window, LayeredCostmap::updateMap() leaves the bounds
#   inverted (they start at max/lowest, nav2_costmap_2d/src/layered_costmap.cpp)
#   and the `if (xn >= x0 && yn >= y0)` guard around every filter's updateCosts()
#   is never satisfied. The stack comes up, spins, publishes a costmap, and drives
#   the filter ZERO times while looking healthy.
# 
# `static_layer` + `rolling_window: true` declares the full window on EVERY cycle
# (nav2_costmap_2d/plugins/static_layer.cpp:393-406). Non-rolling it declares
# bounds only when the map changed (:385-388) -- which would drive the filter once
# and then never again. That is why the demo costmap rolls.
# 
# 255 = free, 0 = occupied, read as `mode: trinary` with `negate: 0`. The one wall
# block is clear of the zone so nothing about it affects what the filter reports.
